# ============================================================================
# PocketCI — .gitignore
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Golden rule of gitignore: we ignore GENERATED things and SECRETS.
# If a file can be regenerated by a build, it doesn't belong in git.
# If a file IS a secret, it must NEVER touch git.
# Everything below is organized by "what disaster does this line prevent?"
# ============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BUILD OUTPUT — the cardinal sin: committing build artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `.gradle/` = Gradle's local project cache (task graph hashes, transformed
# jars for THIS machine's JDK). It regenerates every sync. Committing it
# bloats the repo by tens of MB and causes "could not resolve" errors on
# machines with a different Java version. Classic student repo smell.
.gradle/

# `build/` = actual build output (compiled classes, merged resources, APKs,
# AARs) for every module: /build, /app/build, any future :core/build.
build/

# `app/release/` — even though it's inside build/ (already ignored), we list
# it explicitly as a belt-and-suspenders: people sometimes configure a custom
# output dir, and signed release APKs must NEVER leak into version control.
# A signed APK + its keystore in git = anyone with repo read access can push
# an "update" to your users. Treat signed APKs like the keystore itself.
app/release/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MACHINE-SPECIFIC CONFIG
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `local.properties` is generated by Android Studio/AGP and contains THE SDK
# PATH of whoever synced last. Your path is /home/aomsin/Android/sdk (or a
# Termux path); your teammate's is C:\Users\them\AppData\...\; CI's is
# /usr/local/android-sdk. Commit it and every other machine's build breaks
# with "SDK location not found" — silently, confusingly, and repeatedly.
local.properties

# `*.iml` = IntelliJ module files. One per module, regenerated by Gradle sync.
# They contain absolute paths. Committing them = constant git noise.
*.iml

# `.idea/` = the entire Android Studio project metadata (code style, run
# configurations, inspection profiles). Two people opening the same project
# will fight over these files forever. Let each machine keep its own.
# EXCEPTION some teams commit a trimmed .idea (codeStyles/ only). We're not
# that team yet — keep it simple.
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — if these end up in git, consider them BURNED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `*.jks` / `*.keystore` = signing keys. Phase 42 (ApkSigner) reads a keystore
# to sign CI-built APKs. If this file lands in git history:
#   1. anyone with repo read access can sign APKs as YOU
#   2. even if you delete it later, git HISTORY keeps it — it later, git HISTORY keeps it — rotation is the
#      only fix (new key = new app identity = Play Store "new app")
# Store the real keystore in Termux private storage / a password manager.
*.jks
*.keystore

# `keystore.properties` = the companion file holding storePassword /
# keyPassword that Phase 42 loads at sign time. Passwords and keys travel
# together or not at all — neither goes to git.
keystore.properties

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS / EDITOR NOISE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS Finder leaves these in every folder you open. They commit nothing
# but diff spam.
.DS_Store

# Windows thumbnail cache, if you ever edit from a PC folder.
Thumbs.db

# Vim/emacs swap files — you'll edit in Termux sooner or later; nano doesn't
# make these but vim does.
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TERMUX-SPECIFIC TRAPS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Termux home is not a normal path; if you clone INTO shared storage
# (/sdcard/...) git will scream about file permissions and you'll be tempted
# to add garbage rules to shut it up. Don't. Clone into:
#   ~/pocketci        (private app storage — fast, correct permissions)
# and only COPY files to shared storage when needed. If you must work in
# /sdcard, that's an Android FUSE limitation, not a gitignore problem.

# Gradle wrapper dists download to ~/.gradle — that's OUTSIDE the repo, so
# no rule needed here. Just don't run `gradle wrapper --gradle-version X`
# with a broken network mid-download; you'll get a half-downloaded dist
# and confusing "distribution corrupted" errors (fix: delete ~/.gradle/
# wrapper/dists and retry on Wi-Fi).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT WE DELIBERATELY DO NOT IGNORE (and why)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar  → tiny, required for reproducible builds
#                                    on any machine. Commit it. Always.
# gradlew / gradlew.bat              → same reason. Scripts, small, portable.
# *.kt / *.xml / docs / scripts      → the actual project, obviously.
# app/src/main/res/mipmap-*          → once we add icons (Phase 7+ note),
#                                    they MUST be committed or release builds
#                                    fail with "resource mipmap/ic_launcher
#                                    not found".
